    "result_text": "The build passes green. Here's what I changed to implement the new `customerCode` format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the sole computation site. Now derives:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `owner.getCity()`\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name (unchanged)\n- `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the owners already stored in that same city (was a global count), computed by filtering `ownerRepository.findAll()` on city (case-insensitive)\n\nResult format string is now `\"%s-%s-%04d\"`, e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007`.\n\n**Derived values rebuilt automatically:** `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` wraps whatever `customerCode` holds (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it now emits `SYD-SMI-0007-M26` with no logic change \u2014 I only refreshed its Javadoc example.\n\n**Docs kept consistent:** updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml`, and the two Javadoc blocks.\n\n**Tests:** the new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting the response matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
